  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Rhino &amp; Tiger Postal Fund</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">&quot;The purpose of this project is to empower local community representatives in monitoring tigers, their prey and their habitats and in establishing baseline information on other wildlife and habitats; and establishing a collaborative wildlife protection system between local communities, the Forest Department (FD) and the Karen National Union (KNU) and to support the establishment of a protected area...This will be done by: 1) providing training on camera trapping to the local ethnic communities (Karen, Dawei and Mon); 2) conducting a camera trap survey in Myinmoletkhat Key Biodiversity Area (KBA) with these communities; 3) analyzing the data and presenting it to these communities; 4) providing training on threat monitoring and data recording on standardized forms to the local communities, the FD and KNU; 5) establishing collaborative mechanisms between the local communities, FD and KNU to take actions on illegal activities in Myinmoletkhat KBA; 6) supporting the proposed establishment by KNU and FD of a comanaged protected area in Myinmoletkhat KBA; and 7) applying SMART (Spatial Monitoring and Reporting Tool) to assess the spatial distribution of threats in Myinmoletkhat KBA..&quot;</narrative>
  </description>
